# UI: react-native-reusables (NativeWind)

This project’s default UI stack is **react-native-reusables + NativeWind (Tailwind)**.

## Core rules

- **Use `components/ui/*` first**: Prefer `@/components/ui/*` primitives (e.g. `Button`, `Text`) over ad-hoc components.
- **Style via `className`**: Use NativeWind classes and theme tokens (e.g. `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`).
- **Avoid new `StyleSheet` / inline styles** for UI composition. Keep existing ones, but new work should default to `className` unless you need non-trivial dynamic styles.
- **Don’t use React Native’s built-in `Button`**. Use `@/components/ui/button`.
- **Variants over forks**: If a component needs visual options, add a `variant` / `size` using `cva` in `components/ui/*`.
- **Theme tokens only**: When choosing colors, use CSS variables-backed tokens (Tailwind `colors` in `tailwind.config.js`) instead of hardcoded hex.

## Imports & file layout

- **Imports**:
  - `Button`: `import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'`
  - `Text`: `import { Text } from '@/components/ui/text'`
  - class merge helper: `import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'`
- **UI component location**: `components/ui/<component>.tsx`
- **Non-UI shared utilities**: `lib/*`

## Examples

### Button + Text (preferred)

```tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { Text } from '@/components/ui/text';

export function SaveCTA({ onPress, disabled }: { onPress: () => void; disabled?: boolean }) {
  return (
    <Button variant="default" size="default" disabled={disabled} onPress={onPress}>
      <Text>Lưu</Text>
    </Button>
  );
}
```

### Avoid hardcoded colors (prefer tokens)

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<Text className="text-muted-foreground">Mô tả</Text>

// ❌ BAD
<Text style={{ color: '#64748B' }}>Mô tả</Text>
```

